# The Corrigida's SERIAL played by tools/serial_bot.py (a 400-ms reaction, the warning at the middle path): the intro
# screen, the lives' box and the end screen of a game survived, all 4 killers shot before they fired.
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame serial --headless --ms 126000 --epoch 800000002 --fix all --input tools/play/serial-corrigida-win.input [--dump DIR]
#
# SERIAL's srand is time(NULL), the epoch (seed 2). A key at 2000 ms takes the intro screen down and
# the game's timers start then (`tools/serial_bot.py --seed 2 --arm 2000 --warn-steps 3 --emit FILE`
# wrote the keys; tools/serial_plan.py's Sim, with `arm`, is the game): 41 shots, 36 good figures, 1
# harmless one and 4 killers hit, all before they fired (the middle shot, `serial_killer_after_middle`):
# 5 lives left, 4300 points. The clock ends the game at 122000; the end screen is up for 3 s and the
# result goes at 125000: a win of 500.
